Treasure rule 6, the default from 11/19 (念誠's pick; docs/proposals/coverage-distribution.md)

An unverified record loses the 69 cap: it keeps its own score, and its order among the others, but cannot be a
treasure (scores.treasure.blocked_by "unverified"). Rules 3-5 stay off; rule 1 (conditional and the 79 cap) waits
for the sec.v2 rescan. This flips schema.UNVERIFIED_CAP, which coverage-scoring-b3v7.patch added with today's rule
as its default, and changes the tests that pinned the 69 cap (renamed or reworded, none removed).

Applies LAST, after coverage-scoring-b3v7.patch (loop/proposals/APPLY.md). The stored scores then no longer match
the rule, so records do not validate until `uv run pickfit score --refresh` rewrites them (offline, no model call,
about a second). Checked on 11/19 in a copy outside every checkout, on integrate/proposals-1119: over the records in
data/software, treasures stay 161; the 217 records at exactly 69.0 spread out (0 left); 214 unverified records lose
their cap and 108 unverified records with a sec.v1 known vulnerability move to the 79 cap (79.0: 150 -> 197); then
the full suite passes (2316 passed).

